IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa23-nouns`

-- coa23-part35-register.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 35 (The registrar of companies), ss 1080 to 1092B,
-- lines 15230-15484 of ukpga-2006-46.txt: the register, its annotation and inspection, protected material, copies,
-- production of records, and the power to require information. Layer 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING as in coa-definitions.l4 and the other coa23 modules (a "no" only
-- where the text says no in its own words; NOTHING for silent, list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside the text,
-- limited by its own wording). Each branch that says no carries -- FALSE-kind (...); each "not covered" -- NOTHING-kind (...).
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. A bare "must" not done is JUST FALSE in a function named for compliance (fork F5).
-- Seam inputs are named as inputs/PLAN.md section 4 names them. Every top-level name begins with its section label.

§ `Part 35 - The registrar of companies: ss 1080 to 1092B`

§§ `s 1080 The register`

DECLARE `s 1080(1) record` IS ONE OF
    `s 1080(1)(a) the information contained in documents delivered to the registrar under any enactment`
    `s 1080(1)(b) certificates issued by the registrar under any enactment`
    `s 1080(1) other records`

-- src:15232 | (1) The registrar shall continue to keep records of—
-- src:15233 | (a) the information contained in documents delivered to the registrar under any enactment,, and
-- src:15234 | (b) certificates issued by the registrar under any enactment.
@ref s 1080(1) The registrar shall continue to keep records (src:15232-15234)
GIVEN r IS A `s 1080(1) record`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1080(1) the registrar must keep records of the matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `s 1080(1) other records` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the two heads are not closed with "only"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The duty as a regulative rule (no time limit is stated). The recipient field is a placeholder.
@ref s 1080(1) The registrar must keep the records (src:15232-15234)
`s 1080(1) the registrar's duty to keep records` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Registrar, Registrar, "keep records of the information contained in documents delivered to the registrar and of certificates issued by the registrar"

-- src:15235 | (2) The records relating to companies are referred to collectively in the Companies Acts as “the register”.
@ref s 1080(2) "the register" (src:15235)
GIVEN `the record is one kept by the registrar under section 1080(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the record relates to companies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1080(2) the record is part of the register` MEANS
    IF `the record is one kept by the registrar under section 1080(1)` AND `the record relates to companies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The records relating to companies are referred to collectively in the Companies Acts as “the register”"

-- src:15236 | (3) Information deriving from an enhanced disclosure document (see section 1078) delivered to the registrar, must be kept by the registrar in electronic form.
@ref s 1080(3) Information from an enhanced disclosure document must be kept in electronic form (src:15236)
GIVEN `the information derives from an enhanced disclosure document delivered to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form in which the registrar keeps it` IS A `Form of document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1080(3) the information is kept as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the information derives from an enhanced disclosure document delivered to the registrar`
    THEN CONSIDER `the form in which the registrar keeps it`
         WHEN `electronic form` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `hard copy form` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Information deriving from an enhanced disclosure document ... must be kept by the registrar in electronic form" (a bare "must" not done: fork F5)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Information deriving from an enhanced disclosure document"

@ref s 1080(3) The registrar must keep the information in electronic form (src:15236)
`s 1080(3) the registrar's duty to keep information from an enhanced disclosure document in electronic form` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Registrar, Registrar, "keep the information deriving from an enhanced disclosure document in electronic form"

-- src:15237 | (4) Subject to that, information contained in documents delivered to the registrar may be recorded and kept in any form the registrar thinks fit, provided it is possible to inspect it and produce a copy of it.
-- src:15238 | This is sufficient compliance with any duty of the registrar to keep, file or register the document or to record the information contained in it.
@ref s 1080(4) Other information may be recorded in any form the registrar thinks fit (src:15237-15238)
GIVEN `the information derives from an enhanced disclosure document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registrar thinks the form fit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is possible to inspect the information and produce a copy of it in that form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1080(4) the information may be recorded and kept in the form` MEANS
    IF `the information derives from an enhanced disclosure document`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to that" (subsection (3) governs information deriving from an enhanced disclosure document)
    ELSE IF NOT `it is possible to inspect the information and produce a copy of it in that form`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provided it is possible to inspect it and produce a copy of it" (a "provided" condition not met)
         ELSE IF `the registrar thinks the form fit`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any form the registrar thinks fit"

@ref s 1080(4) Recording and keeping is sufficient compliance with any duty to keep, file or register (src:15238)
GIVEN `the information is recorded and kept in a form the registrar thinks fit, as subsection (4) allows` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1080(4) the recording and keeping is sufficient compliance with the registrar's duty to keep, file or register the document or to record the information` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the information is recorded and kept in a form the registrar thinks fit, as subsection (4) allows`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This is sufficient compliance" speaks of the recording that subsection (4) allows
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (4) does not decide the case

-- src:15239 | (5) The records kept by the registrar must be such that information relating to a company or other registered body is associated with that body, in such manner as the registrar may determine, so as to enable all the information relating to the body to be retrieved.
@ref s 1080(5) The records must associate information with the body it relates to (src:15239)
GIVEN `information relating to a company or other registered body is associated with that body in a manner the registrar has determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that enables all the information relating to the body to be retrieved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1080(5) the records are such as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `information relating to a company or other registered body is associated with that body in a manner the registrar has determined` AND `that enables all the information relating to the body to be retrieved`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The records kept by the registrar must be such that information relating to a company or other registered body is associated with that body, in such manner as the registrar may determine, so as to enable all the information relating to the body to be retrieved" (a bare "must" not done: fork F5)

§§ `s 1081 Annotation of the register`

DECLARE `s 1081(1) occasion` IS ONE OF
    `s 1081(1)(a) a document is delivered to the registrar`
    `s 1081(1)(c) a document is replaced (whether or not material derived from it is removed)`
    `s 1081(1)(d) material is removed`
    `s 1081(1)(e) a document is rectified under section 859M`
    `s 1081(1)(f) a document is replaced under section 859N`
    `s 1081(1) another occasion`

-- src:15241 | (1) The registrar must place a note in the register recording—
-- src:15242 | (a) the date on which a document is delivered to the registrar;
-- src:15243 | (b) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:15244 | (c) if a document is replaced (whether or not material derived from it is removed), the fact that it has been replaced and the date of delivery of the replacement;
-- src:15245 | (d) if material is removed—
-- src:15246 | (i) what was removed (giving a general description of its contents),
-- src:15247 | (ii) under what power, and
-- src:15248 | (iii) the date on which that was done.
-- src:15249 | (e) if a document is rectified under section 859M, the nature and date of rectification;
-- src:15250 | (f) if a document is replaced under section 859N, the fact that it has been replaced and the date of delivery of the replacement.
@ref s 1081(1) The registrar must place a note in the register (src:15241-15250)
GIVEN o IS A `s 1081(1) occasion`
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF STRING)
`s 1081(1) what the note in the register must record` MEANS
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `s 1081(1)(a) a document is delivered to the registrar` THEN JUST (LIST
        "the date on which the document is delivered to the registrar")
    WHEN `s 1081(1)(c) a document is replaced (whether or not material derived from it is removed)` THEN JUST (LIST
        "the fact that it has been replaced"
      , "the date of delivery of the replacement")
    WHEN `s 1081(1)(d) material is removed` THEN JUST (LIST
        "what was removed (giving a general description of its contents)"
      , "under what power"
      , "the date on which that was done")
    WHEN `s 1081(1)(e) a document is rectified under section 859M` THEN JUST (LIST
        "the nature of the rectification"
      , "the date of the rectification")
    WHEN `s 1081(1)(f) a document is replaced under section 859N` THEN JUST (LIST
        "the fact that it has been replaced"
      , "the date of delivery of the replacement")
    WHEN `s 1081(1) another occasion` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the occasions in subsection (1) are not closed with "only" (subsection (2) lets regulations add others)

@ref s 1081(1) The registrar must place the note (src:15241-15250)
`s 1081(1) the registrar's duty to place a note in the register` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Registrar, Registrar, "place a note in the register recording the matters section 1081(1) requires"

-- s 1081(1)(b) and (1A) are blank in this text. s 1081(2) and (7) confer a power to make regulations and fix their procedure: inert (reason 2).

-- src:15255 | (3) No annotation is required in the case of a document that by virtue of section 1072(2) (documents not meeting requirements for proper delivery) is treated as not having been delivered.
@ref s 1081(3) No annotation for a document treated as not delivered (src:15255)
GIVEN `the document is treated as not having been delivered by virtue of section 1072(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1081(3) an annotation is required for the document` MEANS
    IF `the document is treated as not having been delivered by virtue of section 1072(2)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No annotation is required in the case of a document that by virtue of section 1072(2) (documents not meeting requirements for proper delivery) is treated as not having been delivered"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text says only that no annotation is required for that kind of document

-- src:15256 | (4) A note may be removed if it no longer serves any useful purpose.
@ref s 1081(4) A note may be removed if it no longer serves any useful purpose (src:15256)
GIVEN `the note no longer serves any useful purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1081(4) the note may be removed` MEANS
    IF `the note no longer serves any useful purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A note may be removed if it no longer serves any useful purpose": a grant named "may", so a failed "if" is not the text's own "may not" (fork F30)

-- src:15257 | (5) Any duty or power of the registrar with respect to annotation of the register is subject to the court's power under section 1097 (powers of court on ordering removal of material from the register) to direct—
-- src:15258 | (a) that a note be removed from the register, or
-- src:15259 | (b) that no note shall be made of the removal of material that is the subject of the court's order.
@ref s 1081(5) Annotation is subject to the court's power under section 1097 (src:15257-15259)
GIVEN `the court has directed under section 1097 that a note be removed from the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has directed under section 1097 that no note shall be made of the removal of material that is the subject of the court's order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1081(5) the registrar's duty or power with respect to annotation yields to the court's direction` MEANS
    IF `the court has directed under section 1097 that a note be removed from the register` OR `the court has directed under section 1097 that no note shall be made of the removal of material that is the subject of the court's order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to the court's power under section 1097 ... to direct (a) ... or (b) ..." says what yields when the court directs

-- src:15260 | (6) Notes placed in the register in accordance with subsection (1) ..., or in pursuance of regulations under subsection (2) or of any other enactment, are part of the register for all purposes of the Companies Acts.
@ref s 1081(6) Notes are part of the register (src:15260)
GIVEN `the note was placed in the register in accordance with subsection (1), in pursuance of regulations under subsection (2), or in pursuance of any other enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1081(6) the note is part of the register for all purposes of the Companies Acts` MEANS
    IF `the note was placed in the register in accordance with subsection (1), in pursuance of regulations under subsection (2), or in pursuance of any other enactment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Notes placed in the register in accordance with subsection (1) ..., or in pursuance of regulations under subsection (2) or of any other enactment"

§§ `ss 1081A and 1082 Registrar's objectives; unique identifiers`

DECLARE `s 1081A(1) objective` IS ONE OF
    `s 1081A(1) Objective 1 (that any person required to deliver a document to the registrar does so, and that the requirements for proper delivery are complied with)`
    `s 1081A(1) Objective 2 (that information contained in the register is accurate and that the register contains everything it ought to contain)`
    `s 1081A(1) Objective 3 (that records kept by the registrar do not create a false or misleading impression to members of the public)`
    `s 1081A(1) Objective 4 (to prevent companies and others from carrying out unlawful activities or facilitating the carrying out by others of unlawful activities)`
    `s 1081A(1) another aim`

-- src:15263 | (1) The registrar must, in performing the registrar’s functions, seek to promote the following objectives.
-- src:15264 | Objective 1
-- src:15265 | Objective 1 is to ensure that any person who is required to deliver a document to the registrar does so (and that the requirements for proper delivery are complied with).
-- src:15266 | Objective 2
-- src:15267 | Objective 2 is to ensure that information contained in the register is accurate and that the register contains everything it ought to contain.
-- src:15268 | Objective 3
-- src:15269 | Objective 3 is to ensure that records kept by the registrar do not create a false or misleading impression to members of the public.
-- src:15270 | Objective 4
-- src:15271 | Objective 4 is to prevent companies and others from—
-- src:15272 | (a) carrying out unlawful activities, or
-- src:15273 | (b) facilitating the carrying out by others of unlawful activities.
@ref s 1081A(1) The registrar's objectives (src:15263-15273)
GIVEN o IS A `s 1081A(1) objective`
      `the registrar is performing the registrar's functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1081A(1) the registrar must seek to promote the objective` MEANS
    IF `the registrar is performing the registrar's functions`
    THEN CONSIDER o
         WHEN `s 1081A(1) another aim` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the following objectives" are four and the text does not say they are the only aims
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in performing the registrar's functions"

-- The duty as a regulative rule. "Seek to promote" has no time limit and no recipient, so the rule has no WITHIN and the recipient is a placeholder.
@ref s 1081A(1) The registrar must seek to promote the objectives (src:15263-15273)
`s 1081A(1) the registrar's duty to seek to promote the objectives` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Registrar, Registrar, "seek to promote the four objectives of section 1081A(1) in performing the registrar's functions"

-- src:15274 | (2) In Objective 2 the reference to “the register” includes any records kept by the registrar under any enactment.
@ref s 1081A(2) "the register" in Objective 2 (src:15274)
GIVEN `the records are kept by the registrar under any enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1081A(2) the reference to the register in Objective 2 includes the records` MEANS
    IF `the records are kept by the registrar under any enactment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the reference to “the register” includes any records kept by the registrar under any enactment"

DECLARE `s 1082(1) holder of a position` IS ONE OF
    `s 1082(1)(a) a director of a company`
    `s 1082(1)(b) the secretary (or a joint secretary) of a company`
    `s 1082(1)(ba) an authorised corporate service provider`
    `s 1082(1)(bb) an individual whose identity is verified`
    `s 1082(1)(c) in the case of an overseas company whose particulars are registered under section 1046, a person who holds a position specified by regulations under that section`
    `s 1082(1) another position`

-- src:15276 | (1) The Secretary of State may by regulations make provision for the use, in connection with the register or dealings with the registrar, of reference numbers (“unique identifiers”) to identify each person who—
-- src:15277 | (a) is a director of a company,
-- src:15278 | (b) is secretary (or a joint secretary) of a company,
-- src:15279 | (ba) is an authorised corporate service provider;
-- src:15280 | (bb) is an individual whose identity is verified, or
-- src:15281 | (c) in the case of an overseas company whose particulars are registered under section 1046, holds any such position as may be specified for the purposes of this section by regulations under that section.
@ref s 1082(1) "unique identifiers" (src:15276-15281)
GIVEN p IS A `s 1082(1) holder of a position`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1082(1) regulations may provide for a unique identifier to identify the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `s 1082(1) another position` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the heads are not closed with "only"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 1082(2) to (5) confer powers to make regulations, and fix their procedure: inert (reason 2).

§§ `s 1083 Preservation of original documents`

-- Fork F14: the text of s 1083(1) carries two versions of its last words: "This is subject to section 1087(3) (extent of obligation to retain material
-- not available for public inspection). This is subject to— (a) section 1087(3) ...; (b) section 16A(2) of the Limited Partnerships Act 1907 ...; (c) section 22(5) of the Economic
-- Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022 ...". Taken: the list governs (it repeats the older sentence as its limb (a)). Fork F15: the two years
-- are counted to the second anniversary of the day of receipt, and destruction is allowed from the day after.
-- src:15295 | (1) The originals of documents delivered to the registrar in hard copy form must be kept for two years after they are received by the registrar, after which they may be destroyed provided the information contained in them has been recorded.
-- src:15296 | This is subject to section 1087(3) (extent of obligation to retain material not available for public inspection). This is subject to—
-- src:15297 | (a) section 1087(3) (extent of obligation to retain material not available for public inspection);
-- src:15298 | (b) section 16A(2) of the Limited Partnerships Act 1907 (extent of obligation to retain material not available for public inspection);
-- src:15299 | (c) section 22(5) of the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022 (extent of obligation to retain material not available for public inspection).
@ref s 1083(1) Originals of hard copy documents are kept for two years (src:15295-15299)
GIVEN `the original was delivered to the registrar in hard copy form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the registrar received it` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the information contained in it has been recorded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provision named in section 1083(1)(a) to (c) limits the obligation to keep the original` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1083(1) the registrar may destroy the original` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the original was delivered to the registrar in hard copy form`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The originals of documents delivered to the registrar in hard copy form"
    ELSE IF `a provision named in section 1083(1)(a) to (c) limits the obligation to keep the original`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This is subject to" the three provisions named
         ELSE IF `the day in question` AT MOST (Date (DATE_DAY `the day the registrar received it`) (DATE_MONTH `the day the registrar received it`) ((DATE_YEAR `the day the registrar received it`) PLUS 2))
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The originals of documents delivered to the registrar in hard copy form must be kept for two years after they are received by the registrar" (a period the text fixes in its own words: ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))
              ELSE IF `the information contained in it has been recorded`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after which they may be destroyed provided the information contained in them has been recorded" (a "provided" condition not met)

-- The duty to keep as a regulative rule. The two years are counted by the function above, in dates; the rule has no WITHIN because the text states a period of years, not a number of days.
@ref s 1083(1) The registrar must keep the originals (src:15295)
`s 1083(1) the registrar's duty to keep the original of a hard copy document` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Registrar, Registrar, "keep the original of a document delivered in hard copy form for two years after it is received"

-- src:15300 | (2) The registrar is under no obligation to keep the originals of documents delivered in electronic form, provided the information contained in them has been recorded.
@ref s 1083(2) No obligation to keep originals delivered in electronic form (src:15300)
GIVEN `the original was delivered to the registrar in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information contained in it has been recorded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1083(2) the registrar is under no obligation to keep the original` MEANS
    IF `the original was delivered to the registrar in electronic form`
    THEN IF `the information contained in it has been recorded`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registrar is under no obligation to keep the originals of documents delivered in electronic form, provided the information contained in them has been recorded" (a "provided" condition not met)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "documents delivered in electronic form"

-- s 1083(3) says to which documents the section applies in time (documents held when it came into force and later ones): a transitional provision that affects no one now, inert (reason 2).

§§ `ss 1084 and 1084A Records of dissolved companies; optional information`

DECLARE `s 1084(1) occasion` IS ONE OF
    `s 1084(1)(a) a company is dissolved`
    `s 1084(1)(b) an overseas company ceases to have any connection with the United Kingdom by virtue of which it is required to register particulars under section 1046`
    `s 1084(1)(c) a credit or financial institution ceases to be within section 1050 (overseas institutions required to file accounts with the registrar)`
    `s 1084(1) another occasion`

-- src:15303 | (1) This section applies where—
-- src:15304 | (a) a company is dissolved,
-- src:15305 | (b) an overseas company ceases to have any connection with the United Kingdom by virtue of which it is required to register particulars under section 1046, or
-- src:15306 | (c) a credit or financial institution ceases to be within section 1050 (overseas institutions required to file accounts with the registrar),
-- src:15307 | and a reference in this section to “the relevant date” is to the date on which the company was dissolved, the overseas company ceased to have that connection with the United Kingdom or the institution ceased to be within section 1050.
@ref s 1084(1) Records relating to companies that have been dissolved etc: when the section applies (src:15303-15307)
GIVEN o IS A `s 1084(1) occasion`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1084(1) this section applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `s 1084(1) another occasion` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where— (a) ... (b) ... (c) ..." (a failed "where", ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 1084(1) "the relevant date" (src:15303-15307)
GIVEN o IS A `s 1084(1) occasion`
      `the date on which the company was dissolved, the overseas company ceased to have that connection or the institution ceased to be within section 1050` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 1084(1) the relevant date` MEANS
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `s 1084(1) another occasion` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the relevant date is defined only for the three occasions
    OTHERWISE JUST `the date on which the company was dissolved, the overseas company ceased to have that connection or the institution ceased to be within section 1050`

-- src:15308 | (1A) The registrar need not make any information contained in records relating to the company or institution available for public inspection at any time after the end of the period of 20 years beginning with the relevant date.
@ref s 1084(1A) The registrar need not make information available after twenty years (src:15308)
GIVEN `the relevant date` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1084(1A) the registrar need not make the information available for public inspection on the day` MEANS
    IF `the day in question` GREATER THAN (Date (DATE_DAY `the relevant date`) (DATE_MONTH `the relevant date`) ((DATE_YEAR `the relevant date`) PLUS 20)) MINUS 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any time after the end of the period of 20 years beginning with the relevant date" (a period the text fixes in its own words: ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))

-- src:15309 | (2) The registrar of companies for England and Wales may, at any time after the period of two years beginning with the relevant date, direct that any records relating to the company or institution that are held by the registrar are to be removed to the Public Record Office.
@ref s 1084(2) The registrar for England and Wales may direct removal of records to the Public Record Office (src:15309)
GIVEN `the relevant date` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1084(2) the registrar of companies for England and Wales may direct that the records be removed to the Public Record Office on the day` MEANS
    IF `the day in question` GREATER THAN (Date (DATE_DAY `the relevant date`) (DATE_MONTH `the relevant date`) ((DATE_YEAR `the relevant date`) PLUS 2)) MINUS 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any time after the period of two years beginning with the relevant date" (a period the text fixes in its own words: ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))

-- src:15310 | (2AA) The registrar of companies for Northern Ireland may, at any time after the period of two years beginning with the relevant date, direct that any records relating to the company or institution that are held by the registrar are to be removed to the Public Record Office of Northern Ireland.
@ref s 1084(2AA) The registrar for Northern Ireland may direct removal of records to the Public Record Office of Northern Ireland (src:15310)
GIVEN `the relevant date` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1084(2AA) the registrar of companies for Northern Ireland may direct that the records be removed to the Public Record Office of Northern Ireland on the day` MEANS
    IF `the day in question` GREATER THAN (Date (DATE_DAY `the relevant date`) (DATE_MONTH `the relevant date`) ((DATE_YEAR `the relevant date`) PLUS 2)) MINUS 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any time after the period of two years beginning with the relevant date" (a period the text fixes in its own words: ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))

-- Finding: s 1084(3) refers to "subsection (2) or (2A)", and this text has (2) and (2AA) but no (2A). The reference is carried as written; the function reads it as both directions.
-- src:15311 | (3) Records in respect of which a direction is given under subsection (2) or (2A) are to be disposed of under the enactments relating to the Public Record Office or, as the case may be, the Public Record Office of Northern Ireland.
@ref s 1084(3) Records subject to a direction are disposed of under the Public Record Office enactments (src:15311)
GIVEN `a direction was given under subsection (2) or (2A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1084(3) the records are to be disposed of under the enactments relating to the Public Record Office` MEANS
    IF `a direction was given under subsection (2) or (2A)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Records in respect of which a direction is given under subsection (2) or (2A)"

-- src:15312 | (4) In subsection (1)(a) “company” includes a company provisionally or completely registered under the Joint Stock Companies Act 1844 (c. 110).
@ref s 1084(4) "company" in subsection (1)(a) includes a company registered under the Joint Stock Companies Act 1844 (src:15312)
GIVEN `the company is provisionally or completely registered under the Joint Stock Companies Act 1844` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1084(4) the body is a company for the purposes of subsection (1)(a)` MEANS
    IF `the company is provisionally or completely registered under the Joint Stock Companies Act 1844`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "In subsection (1)(a) “company” includes a company provisionally or completely registered under the Joint Stock Companies Act 1844"

-- s 1084(4A) and (5) are blank in this text.

-- src:15317 | (2) In this section “ optional information ”, in relation to a company or other body, means information about the company or body which, but for the regulations, the company or body would not be obliged or authorised under any enactment to deliver to the registrar.
@ref s 1084A(2) "optional information" (src:15317)
GIVEN `the information is about the company or body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `but for the regulations the company or body would not be obliged under any enactment to deliver it to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `but for the regulations the company or body would not be authorised under any enactment to deliver it to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1084A(2) the information is optional information` MEANS
    IF       `the information is about the company or body`
        AND  `but for the regulations the company or body would not be obliged under any enactment to deliver it to the registrar`
        AND  `but for the regulations the company or body would not be authorised under any enactment to deliver it to the registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“optional information”, in relation to a company or other body, means information about the company or body which, but for the regulations, the company or body would not be obliged or authorised under any enactment to deliver to the registrar"

-- s 1084A(1), (3) and (4) confer powers to make regulations, and fix their procedure: inert (reason 2).

§§ `ss 1085 and 1086 Inspection and copies`

-- src:15324 | (1) Any person may inspect the register.
@ref s 1085(1) Any person may inspect the register (src:15324)
GIVEN `the material forms part of the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1085(3) a provision named in subsection (3) restricts inspection of the material` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1085(1) the person may inspect the material on the register` MEANS
    IF `the material forms part of the register`
    THEN CONSIDER `s 1085(3) a provision named in subsection (3) restricts inspection of the material`
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section has effect subject to" the provisions named in subsection (3)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether a provision named in subsection (3) restricts inspection is decided by that provision
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person may inspect the register"

@ref s 1085(1) Any person may inspect the register (src:15324)
`s 1085(1) the right of any person to inspect the register` MEANS
    PARTY `s 1065 any person`
    MAY `s 1085 inspect the register`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:15325 | (2) The right of inspection extends to the originals of documents delivered to the registrar in hard copy form if, and only if, the record kept by the registrar of the contents of the document is illegible or unavailable.
-- src:15326 | The period for which such originals are to be kept is limited by section 1083(1).
@ref s 1085(2) The right of inspection extends to originals if, and only if, the record is illegible or unavailable (src:15325-15326)
GIVEN `the original was delivered to the registrar in hard copy form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the record kept by the registrar of its contents is illegible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the record kept by the registrar of its contents is unavailable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1085(2) the right of inspection extends to the original` MEANS
    IF `the original was delivered to the registrar in hard copy form`
    THEN IF `the record kept by the registrar of its contents is illegible` OR `the record kept by the registrar of its contents is unavailable`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if, and only if, the record kept by the registrar of the contents of the document is illegible or unavailable"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the originals of documents delivered to the registrar in hard copy form"

-- src:15332 | (1) Any person may require a copy of any material on the register that is available for public inspection.
@ref s 1086(1) Any person may require a copy of material available for public inspection (src:15332)
GIVEN `the material is on the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the material is available for public inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1086(1) the person may require a copy of the material` MEANS
    IF `the material is on the register` AND `the material is available for public inspection`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any material on the register that is available for public inspection"

@ref s 1086(1) Any person may require a copy (src:15332)
`s 1086(1) the right of any person to a copy of material on the register` MEANS
    PARTY `s 1065 any person`
    MAY `s 1086 require a copy of material on the register`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:15333 | (2) The fee for any such copy of material derived from an enhanced disclosure document (see section 1078), whether in hard copy or electronic form, must not exceed the administrative cost of providing it.
@ref s 1086(2) The fee for a copy of enhanced disclosure document material (src:15333)
GIVEN `the copy is of material derived from an enhanced disclosure document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fee charged for the copy, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the administrative cost of providing the copy, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1086(2) the fee complies with the limit` MEANS
    IF `the copy is of material derived from an enhanced disclosure document`
    THEN IF `the fee charged for the copy, in pounds` AT MOST `the administrative cost of providing the copy, in pounds`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The fee for any such copy of material derived from an enhanced disclosure document, whether in hard copy or electronic form, must not exceed the administrative cost of providing it"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "material derived from an enhanced disclosure document"

-- s 1085(3) lists provisions to which section 1085 is subject: it is carried by the second input of s 1085(1), whose answer the seat takes from s 1084(1A) and s 1087.
-- s 1085(2)'s second sentence ("The period for which such originals are to be kept is limited by section 1083(1)") is a cross-reference to s 1083(1): inert (reason 1).
-- s 1086(3) is blank in this text.

§§ `ss 1087 to 1087C Material not available for public inspection`

DECLARE `s 1087(1) kind of material` IS ONE OF
    `s 1087(1)(za(i)) an email address delivered to the registrar under section 9(5)(aa) or 88B (initial registered email address and change of address)`
    `s 1087(1)(za(ii)) an email address delivered to the registrar under section 30 of the Economic Crime and Corporate Transparency Act 2023 (company's registered email address: transitional provision)`
    `s 1087(1)(a) the contents of any document sent to the registrar containing views expressed pursuant to section 56 (comments on proposal by company to use certain words or expressions in company name)`
    `s 1087(1)(aa) any application or other document delivered to the registrar under regulations under section 120A (protection of individual membership information)`
    `s 1087(1)(b) protected information within section 242(1) (directors' residential addresses: restriction on disclosure by registrar) or any corresponding provision of regulations under section 1046 (overseas companies)`
    `s 1087(1)(ba(i)) representations received by the registrar in response to a notice under section 245(2) (notice of proposal to put director's usual residential address on the public record)`
    `s 1087(1)(ba(ii)) representations received by the registrar in response to a notice under any corresponding provision of regulations under section 1046 (overseas companies)`
    `s 1087(1)(bb) information to which sections 240 to 244 are applied by section 790ZF(1) (residential addresses of people with significant control over the company) or any corresponding provision of regulations under section 1046 (overseas companies)`
    `s 1087(1)(bba(i)) any application or other document delivered to the registrar under regulations under section 468A (regulations protecting profit and loss accounts for certain companies)`
    `s 1087(1)(bba(ii)) any information which regulations under section 468A require not to be made available for public inspection`
    `s 1087(1)(bc) any application or other document delivered to the registrar under regulations under section 790ZG (protection of PSC information)`
    `s 1087(1)(c) any application to the registrar under section 1024 (application for administrative restoration to the register) that has not yet been determined or was not successful`
    `s 1087(1)(d) any document received by the registrar in connection with the giving or withdrawal of consent under section 1075 (informal correction of documents) before the repeal of that section by the Economic Crime and Corporate Transparency Act 2023`
    `s 1087(1)(dza) any statement made in accordance with regulations made by virtue of section 1082(2)(c)`
    `s 1087(1)(da) relevant date of birth information that section 1087A provides is not to be made available for public inspection`
    `s 1087(1)(e(i)) any application or other document delivered to the registrar under regulations under section 1088 (regulations protecting material), other than information provided by virtue of section 1088(5)`
    `s 1087(1)(e(ii)) any information which regulations under section 1088 require not to be made available for public inspection`
    `s 1087(1)(ea) any information provided to the registrar under section 1092A (power to require further information)`
    `s 1087(1)(f) any application or other document delivered to the registrar under section 1094 (removal of material from the register)`
    `s 1087(1)(g) any court order under section 1096 (rectification of the register under court order) that the court has directed under section 1097 is not to be made available for public inspection`
    `s 1087(1)(ga) any application or other document delivered to the registrar under section 1097A, 1097B or 1097C (rectification of registered office, service address or principal office address) other than an order or direction of the court`
    `s 1087(1)(gb) any application or other document delivered to the registrar under section 1098B, 1098D or 1098E or regulations under section 1098G (authorised corporate service providers)`
    `s 1087(1)(gc) any document delivered to the registrar under regulations under section 1110B`
    `s 1087(1)(gd, section 12(2A)) a statement or other document delivered to the registrar by virtue of section 12(2A) (identity verification)`
    `s 1087(1)(gd, section 12B(2) to (4)) a statement or other document delivered to the registrar by virtue of section 12B(2) to (4) (identity verification)`
    `s 1087(1)(gd, section 167G(3)(c)) a statement or other document delivered to the registrar by virtue of section 167G(3)(c) (identity verification)`
    `s 1087(1)(gd, section 790LB(1) to (3)) a statement or other document delivered to the registrar by virtue of section 790LB(1) to (3) (identity verification)`
    `s 1087(1)(gd, section 790LM(2)) a statement or other document delivered to the registrar by virtue of section 790LM(2) (identity verification)`
    `s 1087(1)(gd, section 790LN(2)) a statement or other document delivered to the registrar by virtue of section 790LN(2) (identity verification)`
    `s 1087(1)(gd, section 790LO(2)) a statement or other document delivered to the registrar by virtue of section 790LO(2) (identity verification)`
    `s 1087(1)(gd, section 790LP(2)) a statement or other document delivered to the registrar by virtue of section 790LP(2) (identity verification)`
    `s 1087(1)(gd, section 790LS(1) to (3)) a statement or other document delivered to the registrar by virtue of section 790LS(1) to (3) (identity verification)`
    `s 1087(1)(gd, section 1067A) a statement or other document delivered to the registrar by virtue of section 1067A (identity verification)`
    `s 1087(1)(i) any e-mail address, identification code or password deriving from a document delivered for the purpose of authorising or facilitating electronic filing procedures or providing information by telephone`
    `s 1087(1)(j(i)) the contents of any documents held by the registrar pending a decision of the Regulator of Community Interest Companies under section 36A of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004 (eligibility for registration as community interest company), that the registrar is not later required to record`
    `s 1087(1)(j(ii)) the contents of any documents held by the registrar pending a decision of the Regulator of Community Interest Companies under section 38 of that Act (eligibility for conversion to community interest company), that the registrar is not later required to record`
    `s 1087(1)(j(iii)) the contents of any documents held by the registrar pending a decision of the Regulator of Community Interest Companies under section 55 of that Act (eligibility for conversion from community interest company to charity), that the registrar is not later required to record`
    `s 1087(1)(ja) any record of the information contained in a document (or part of a document) mentioned in any of the previous paragraphs of this subsection`
    `s 1087(1)(k) any other material excluded from public inspection by or under any other enactment`
    `s 1087(1) other material`

-- (h) is blank in this text. The list is not closed with "only" (paragraph (k) hands the rest to other enactments), so material in none of the heads is not decided.
