-- src:15374 | section 1067A;
-- src:15376 | (i) any e-mail address, identification code or password deriving from a document delivered for the purpose of authorising or facilitating electronic filing procedures or providing information by telephone;
-- src:15377 | (j) the contents of any documents held by the registrar pending a decision of the Regulator of Community Interest Companies under—
-- src:15378 | (i) section 36A of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004 (eligibility for registration as community interest company),
-- src:15379 | (ii) section 38 of that Act (eligibility for conversion to community interest company), or
-- src:15380 | (iii) section 55 of that Act (eligibility for conversion from community interest company to charity),
-- src:15381 | and that the registrar is not later required to record;
-- src:15382 | (ja) any record of the information contained in a document (or part of a document) mentioned in any of the previous paragraphs of this subsection;
-- src:15383 | (k) any other material excluded from public inspection by or under any other enactment.
@ref s 1087(1) Material not available for public inspection (src:15336-15383)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 1087(1) kind of material`
      `the material forms part of the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1087(1) the registrar must not make the material available for public inspection` MEANS
    IF `the material forms part of the register`
    THEN CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `s 1087(1) other material` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the heads of subsection (1) are not closed with "only"; the rest is for other enactments (paragraph (k))
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "so far as it forms part of the register"

-- Which head a person means, named by its paragraph as the text prints it (for example za(i), b, ba(ii) or gd, section 12(2A)).
@ref s 1087(1) Material not available for public inspection: the head named by its paragraph (src:15336-15383)
GIVEN `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` IS A STRING
GIVETH A `s 1087(1) kind of material`
`s 1087(1) the head of the list named by its paragraph` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "za(i)" THEN `s 1087(1)(za(i)) an email address delivered to the registrar under section 9(5)(aa) or 88B (initial registered email address and change of address)`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "za(ii)" THEN `s 1087(1)(za(ii)) an email address delivered to the registrar under section 30 of the Economic Crime and Corporate Transparency Act 2023 (company's registered email address: transitional provision)`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "a" THEN `s 1087(1)(a) the contents of any document sent to the registrar containing views expressed pursuant to section 56 (comments on proposal by company to use certain words or expressions in company name)`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "aa" THEN `s 1087(1)(aa) any application or other document delivered to the registrar under regulations under section 120A (protection of individual membership information)`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "b" THEN `s 1087(1)(b) protected information within section 242(1) (directors' residential addresses: restriction on disclosure by registrar) or any corresponding provision of regulations under section 1046 (overseas companies)`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "ba(i)" THEN `s 1087(1)(ba(i)) representations received by the registrar in response to a notice under section 245(2) (notice of proposal to put director's usual residential address on the public record)`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "ba(ii)" THEN `s 1087(1)(ba(ii)) representations received by the registrar in response to a notice under any corresponding provision of regulations under section 1046 (overseas companies)`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "bb" THEN `s 1087(1)(bb) information to which sections 240 to 244 are applied by section 790ZF(1) (residential addresses of people with significant control over the company) or any corresponding provision of regulations under section 1046 (overseas companies)`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "bba(i)" THEN `s 1087(1)(bba(i)) any application or other document delivered to the registrar under regulations under section 468A (regulations protecting profit and loss accounts for certain companies)`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "bba(ii)" THEN `s 1087(1)(bba(ii)) any information which regulations under section 468A require not to be made available for public inspection`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "bc" THEN `s 1087(1)(bc) any application or other document delivered to the registrar under regulations under section 790ZG (protection of PSC information)`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "c" THEN `s 1087(1)(c) any application to the registrar under section 1024 (application for administrative restoration to the register) that has not yet been determined or was not successful`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "d" THEN `s 1087(1)(d) any document received by the registrar in connection with the giving or withdrawal of consent under section 1075 (informal correction of documents) before the repeal of that section by the Economic Crime and Corporate Transparency Act 2023`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "dza" THEN `s 1087(1)(dza) any statement made in accordance with regulations made by virtue of section 1082(2)(c)`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "da" THEN `s 1087(1)(da) relevant date of birth information that section 1087A provides is not to be made available for public inspection`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "e(i)" THEN `s 1087(1)(e(i)) any application or other document delivered to the registrar under regulations under section 1088 (regulations protecting material), other than information provided by virtue of section 1088(5)`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "e(ii)" THEN `s 1087(1)(e(ii)) any information which regulations under section 1088 require not to be made available for public inspection`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "ea" THEN `s 1087(1)(ea) any information provided to the registrar under section 1092A (power to require further information)`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "f" THEN `s 1087(1)(f) any application or other document delivered to the registrar under section 1094 (removal of material from the register)`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "g" THEN `s 1087(1)(g) any court order under section 1096 (rectification of the register under court order) that the court has directed under section 1097 is not to be made available for public inspection`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "ga" THEN `s 1087(1)(ga) any application or other document delivered to the registrar under section 1097A, 1097B or 1097C (rectification of registered office, service address or principal office address) other than an order or direction of the court`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "gb" THEN `s 1087(1)(gb) any application or other document delivered to the registrar under section 1098B, 1098D or 1098E or regulations under section 1098G (authorised corporate service providers)`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "gc" THEN `s 1087(1)(gc) any document delivered to the registrar under regulations under section 1110B`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "gd, section 12(2A)" THEN `s 1087(1)(gd, section 12(2A)) a statement or other document delivered to the registrar by virtue of section 12(2A) (identity verification)`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "gd, section 12B(2) to (4)" THEN `s 1087(1)(gd, section 12B(2) to (4)) a statement or other document delivered to the registrar by virtue of section 12B(2) to (4) (identity verification)`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "gd, section 167G(3)(c)" THEN `s 1087(1)(gd, section 167G(3)(c)) a statement or other document delivered to the registrar by virtue of section 167G(3)(c) (identity verification)`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "gd, section 790LB(1) to (3)" THEN `s 1087(1)(gd, section 790LB(1) to (3)) a statement or other document delivered to the registrar by virtue of section 790LB(1) to (3) (identity verification)`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "gd, section 790LM(2)" THEN `s 1087(1)(gd, section 790LM(2)) a statement or other document delivered to the registrar by virtue of section 790LM(2) (identity verification)`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "gd, section 790LN(2)" THEN `s 1087(1)(gd, section 790LN(2)) a statement or other document delivered to the registrar by virtue of section 790LN(2) (identity verification)`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "gd, section 790LO(2)" THEN `s 1087(1)(gd, section 790LO(2)) a statement or other document delivered to the registrar by virtue of section 790LO(2) (identity verification)`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "gd, section 790LP(2)" THEN `s 1087(1)(gd, section 790LP(2)) a statement or other document delivered to the registrar by virtue of section 790LP(2) (identity verification)`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "gd, section 790LS(1) to (3)" THEN `s 1087(1)(gd, section 790LS(1) to (3)) a statement or other document delivered to the registrar by virtue of section 790LS(1) to (3) (identity verification)`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "gd, section 1067A" THEN `s 1087(1)(gd, section 1067A) a statement or other document delivered to the registrar by virtue of section 1067A (identity verification)`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "i" THEN `s 1087(1)(i) any e-mail address, identification code or password deriving from a document delivered for the purpose of authorising or facilitating electronic filing procedures or providing information by telephone`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "j(i)" THEN `s 1087(1)(j(i)) the contents of any documents held by the registrar pending a decision of the Regulator of Community Interest Companies under section 36A of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004 (eligibility for registration as community interest company), that the registrar is not later required to record`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "j(ii)" THEN `s 1087(1)(j(ii)) the contents of any documents held by the registrar pending a decision of the Regulator of Community Interest Companies under section 38 of that Act (eligibility for conversion to community interest company), that the registrar is not later required to record`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "j(iii)" THEN `s 1087(1)(j(iii)) the contents of any documents held by the registrar pending a decision of the Regulator of Community Interest Companies under section 55 of that Act (eligibility for conversion from community interest company to charity), that the registrar is not later required to record`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "ja" THEN `s 1087(1)(ja) any record of the information contained in a document (or part of a document) mentioned in any of the previous paragraphs of this subsection`
        IF `the paragraph of section 1087(1) as printed` EQUALS "k" THEN `s 1087(1)(k) any other material excluded from public inspection by or under any other enactment`
        OTHERWISE `s 1087(1) other material`

-- src:15384 | (2) Where subsection (1), or a provision referred to in subsection (1), imposes a restriction by reference to material deriving from a particular description of document (or part of a document), that does not affect the availability for public inspection of the same information contained in material derived from another description of document (or part of a document) in relation to which no such restriction applies.
@ref s 1087(2) A restriction by reference to one description of document (src:15384)
GIVEN `the restriction is by reference to material deriving from a particular description of document (or part of a document)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the same information is contained in material derived from another description of document (or part) in relation to which no such restriction applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1087(2) the restriction affects the availability for public inspection of the same information in the other material` MEANS
    IF `the restriction is by reference to material deriving from a particular description of document (or part of a document)` AND `the same information is contained in material derived from another description of document (or part) in relation to which no such restriction applies`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that does not affect the availability for public inspection of the same information contained in material derived from another description of document"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text says only that a restriction by reference to one description of document does not affect the same information in material that carries no such restriction

-- src:15385 | (3) Material to which this section applies need not be retained by the registrar for longer than appears to the registrar reasonably necessary for the purposes for which the material was delivered to the registrar.
@ref s 1087(3) The registrar need not retain material for longer than reasonably necessary (src:15385)
GIVEN `the material is material to which section 1087 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the registrar that retaining it for longer is not reasonably necessary for the purposes for which it was delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1087(3) the registrar need not retain the material for longer` MEANS
    IF `the material is material to which section 1087 applies` AND `it appears to the registrar that retaining it for longer is not reasonably necessary for the purposes for which it was delivered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Material to which this section applies need not be retained by the registrar for longer than appears to the registrar reasonably necessary for the purposes for which the material was delivered"

-- s 1087(1) as a regulative rule: the registrar SHANT make the material available. No time limit is stated.
-- src:15336 | (1) The following material must not , so far as it forms part of the register, be made available by the registrar for public inspection—
@ref s 1087(1) The registrar must not make the material available for public inspection (src:15336)
`s 1087(1) the prohibition on making protected material available for public inspection` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    SHANT `Action of a party` OF Registrar, Registrar, "make material listed in section 1087(1), so far as it forms part of the register, available for public inspection"
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the registrar made material listed in section 1087(1) available for public inspection"

-- s 1087ZA is blank in this text.

DECLARE `s 1087A(3) the person` IS ONE OF
    `s 1087A(3)(a) a director (or proposed director)`
    `s 1087A(3)(b) a registrable person in relation to the company`
    `s 1087A(3) another person`

-- src:15393 | (3) “Relevant date of birth information” means—
-- src:15394 | (a) information as to the day of the month (but not the month or year) on which a director (or proposed director) was born;
-- src:15395 | (b) information as to the day of the month (but not the month or year) on which a registrable person in relation to the company was born.
@ref s 1087A(3) "Relevant date of birth information" (src:15393-15395)
GIVEN p IS A `s 1087A(3) the person`
      `the information is the day of the month on which the person was born, and not the month or year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1087A(3) the information is relevant date of birth information` MEANS
    IF `the information is the day of the month on which the person was born, and not the month or year`
    THEN CONSIDER p
         WHEN `s 1087A(3) another person` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Relevant date of birth information” means— (a) ... a director (or proposed director) ...; (b) ... a registrable person" and the person is neither
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "information as to the day of the month (but not the month or year) on which a director (or proposed director) was born"

-- src:15396 | (4) Information about a director (or proposed director) or registrable person does not cease to be relevant date of birth information when they cease to be a director (or proposed director) or registrable person.
@ref s 1087A(4) The information does not cease to be relevant when the person ceases to be a director or registrable person (src:15396)
GIVEN `the person has ceased to be a director (or proposed director) or registrable person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1087A(4) the information has ceased to be relevant date of birth information` MEANS
    IF `the person has ceased to be a director (or proposed director) or registrable person`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Information about a director (or proposed director) or registrable person does not cease to be relevant date of birth information when they cease to be a director (or proposed director) or registrable person"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text says only that ceasing to hold the position does not end the status

-- src:15398 | (6) In this section “registrable person”, in relation to a company, has the meaning given by section 790C(4).
@ref s 1087A(6) "registrable person" (src:15398)
GIVEN `s 790C(4) the person is a registrable person in relation to the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1087A(6) the person is a registrable person in relation to the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 790C(4) the person is a registrable person in relation to the company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the borrowed definition says no, supplied as an input): "“registrable person”, in relation to a company, has the meaning given by section 790C(4)"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 790C(4) is in another part's range (coa17)

DECLARE `s 1087A(1) material` IS ONE OF
    `s 1087A(1)(a) so much of any document delivered to the registrar as is required to contain relevant date of birth information`
    `s 1087A(1)(b) any record of the information contained in part of a document that is unavailable because of paragraph (a)`
    `s 1087A(1) other material`

-- src:15389 | (1) The registrar must not make available for public inspection—
-- src:15390 | (a) so much of any document delivered to the registrar as is required to contain relevant date of birth information;
-- src:15391 | (b) any record of the information contained in part of a document that is unavailable because of paragraph (a).
@ref s 1087A(1) The registrar must not make date of birth information available (src:15389-15391)
GIVEN m IS A `s 1087A(1) material`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1087A(1) the registrar must not make the material available for public inspection` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN `s 1087A(1) other material` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on the two heads (a) and (b)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 1087A(1) The registrar must not make relevant date of birth information available (src:15389-15391)
`s 1087A(1) the prohibition on making relevant date of birth information available for public inspection` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    SHANT `Action of a party` OF Registrar, Registrar, "make available for public inspection any part of a document required to contain relevant date of birth information"
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the registrar made relevant date of birth information available for public inspection"

-- src:15397 | (5) Subsection (1)(b) does not affect the availability for public inspection of the same information contained in material derived from a part of a document that was not required to contain the information.
@ref s 1087A(5) Subsection (1)(b) does not affect the same information in material from a part not required to contain it (src:15397)
GIVEN `the same information is contained in material derived from a part of a document that was not required to contain the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1087A(5) subsection (1)(b) affects the availability of the same information in that material` MEANS
    IF `the same information is contained in material derived from a part of a document that was not required to contain the information`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1)(b) does not affect the availability for public inspection of the same information contained in material derived from a part of a document that was not required to contain the information"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text says only that (1)(b) does not reach that material

-- s 1087A(2) ("This section has limited application ... see section 1087B") is a signpost: inert (reason 1); section 1087B is encoded below.

DECLARE `s 1087B(3) old document` IS ONE OF
    `s 1087B(3)(a) a statement of a company's proposed officers delivered under section 9 where the subscribers gave notice of election under section 167A in respect of the company's register of directors when the statement was delivered`
    `s 1087B(3)(b) a document delivered by the company under section 167D (duty to notify registrar of changes while election in force)`
    `s 1087B(3)(c) a statement of initial significant control delivered under section 9 where the subscribers gave notice of election under section 790X in respect of the company when the statement was delivered`
    `s 1087B(3)(d) a document containing a statement or updated statement delivered by the company under section 790X(6)(b) or (7)`
    `s 1087B(3)(e) a document delivered by the company under section 790ZA (duty to notify registrar of changes while election in force)`
    `s 1087B(4)(a)(i) a statement of proposed officers delivered under section 9`
    `s 1087B(4)(a)(ii) notice given under section 167 of a person having become a director of the company`
    `s 1087B another old document`

-- src:15400 | (1) This section limits the extent to which section 1087A applies in relation to documents delivered to the registrar before that section comes fully into force (“old documents”).
-- src:15401 | (2) Section 1087A does not apply in relation to any old documents registered before 10 October 2015.
-- src:15402 | (3) Section 1087A does not apply in relation to any old document that is—
-- src:15403 | (a) a statement of a company’s proposed officers delivered under section 9 in circumstances where the subscribers gave notice of election under section 167A (election to keep information on central register) in respect of the company’s register of directors when the statement was delivered;
-- src:15404 | (b) a document delivered by the company under section 167D (duty to notify registrar of changes while election in force);
-- src:15405 | (c) a statement of initial significant control delivered under section 9 in circumstances where the subscribers gave notice of election under section 790X in respect of the company when the statement was delivered;
-- src:15406 | (d) a document containing a statement or updated statement delivered by the company under section 790X(6)(b) or (7) (statement accompanying notice of election made after incorporation);
-- src:15407 | (e) a document delivered by the company under section 790ZA (duty to notify registrar of changes while election in force).
-- src:15408 | (4) Section 1087A does not apply in relation to any old document if—
-- src:15409 | (a) the document is—
-- src:15410 | (i) a statement of proposed officers delivered under section 9, or
-- src:15411 | (ii) notice given under section 167 of a person having become a director of the company,
-- src:15412 | (b) after the delivery of the document an election was made under section 167A in respect of the company’s register of directors, and
-- src:15413 | (c) the relevant date of birth information relates to a person who was a director of the company when that election took effect.
-- src:15414 | (5) References in subsections (3)(a) to (e) and (4)(a) to (c) to a provision of this Act are to the provision as it had effect at the time at which the document was delivered (the provisions in question were repealed by the Economic Crime and Corporate Transparency Act 2023).
@ref s 1087B Protection of date of birth information in old documents (src:15400-15414)
GIVEN `the document was delivered to the registrar before section 1087A came fully into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the document was registered` IS A DATE
      kind IS A `s 1087B(3) old document`
      `after the delivery of the document an election was made under section 167A in respect of the company's register of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant date of birth information relates to a person who was a director of the company when that election took effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1087B section 1087A applies to the old document` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the document was delivered to the registrar before section 1087A came fully into force`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section limits the extent to which section 1087A applies in relation to documents delivered to the registrar before that section comes fully into force (“old documents”)"
    ELSE IF `the day the document was registered` BELOW (Date 10 10 2015)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 1087A does not apply in relation to any old documents registered before 10 October 2015"
         ELSE CONSIDER kind
              WHEN `s 1087B(3)(a) a statement of a company's proposed officers delivered under section 9 where the subscribers gave notice of election under section 167A in respect of the company's register of directors when the statement was delivered` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 1087A does not apply in relation to any old document that is— (a) a statement of a company’s proposed officers delivered under section 9 in circumstances where the subscribers gave notice of election under section 167A"
              WHEN `s 1087B(3)(b) a document delivered by the company under section 167D (duty to notify registrar of changes while election in force)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) a document delivered by the company under section 167D"
              WHEN `s 1087B(3)(c) a statement of initial significant control delivered under section 9 where the subscribers gave notice of election under section 790X in respect of the company when the statement was delivered` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) a statement of initial significant control delivered under section 9 in circumstances where the subscribers gave notice of election under section 790X"
              WHEN `s 1087B(3)(d) a document containing a statement or updated statement delivered by the company under section 790X(6)(b) or (7)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) a document containing a statement or updated statement delivered by the company under section 790X(6)(b) or (7)"
              WHEN `s 1087B(3)(e) a document delivered by the company under section 790ZA (duty to notify registrar of changes while election in force)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(e) a document delivered by the company under section 790ZA"
              WHEN `s 1087B(4)(a)(i) a statement of proposed officers delivered under section 9` THEN
                  IF `after the delivery of the document an election was made under section 167A in respect of the company's register of directors` AND `the relevant date of birth information relates to a person who was a director of the company when that election took effect`
                  THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 1087A does not apply in relation to any old document if— (a) the document is— (i) a statement of proposed officers delivered under section 9, ... (b) after the delivery of the document an election was made under section 167A ..., and (c) the relevant date of birth information relates to a person who was a director of the company when that election took effect"
                  ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say that section 1087A applies to an old document outside the limits (fork F16)
              WHEN `s 1087B(4)(a)(ii) notice given under section 167 of a person having become a director of the company` THEN
                  IF `after the delivery of the document an election was made under section 167A in respect of the company's register of directors` AND `the relevant date of birth information relates to a person who was a director of the company when that election took effect`
                  THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 1087A does not apply in relation to any old document if— (a) the document is— ... (ii) notice given under section 167 of a person having become a director of the company, (b) ... and (c) ..."
                  ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say that section 1087A applies to an old document outside the limits (fork F16)
              WHEN `s 1087B another old document` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say that section 1087A applies to an old document outside the limits (fork F16)

-- src:15414 | (5) References in subsections (3)(a) to (e) and (4)(a) to (c) to a provision of this Act are to the provision as it had effect at the time at which the document was delivered (the provisions in question were repealed by the Economic Crime and Corporate Transparency Act 2023).
@ref s 1087B(5) The references to provisions of the Act are to the provisions as they had effect when the document was delivered (src:15414)
GIVEN `the reference is in subsection (3)(a) to (e) or (4)(a) to (c) to a provision of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1087B(5) the reference is to the provision as it had effect at the time at which the document was delivered` MEANS
    IF `the reference is in subsection (3)(a) to (e) or (4)(a) to (c) to a provision of this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "References in subsections (3)(a) to (e) and (4)(a) to (c) to a provision of this Act"

-- src:15416 | (1) The registrar must not disclose relevant date of birth information except—
-- src:15417 | (a) in accordance with subsection (2) or (3), or
-- src:15418 | (b) as permitted by section 1110F (general powers of disclosure by the registrar).
@ref s 1087C(1) The registrar must not disclose relevant date of birth information except (src:15416-15418)
GIVEN `the information is made available for public inspection (subsection (2))` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is to a credit reference agency (subsection (3))` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1110F the disclosure is permitted by the registrar's general powers of disclosure` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1087C(1) the registrar is barred from disclosing the relevant date of birth information` MEANS
    IF `the information is made available for public inspection (subsection (2))` OR `the disclosure is to a credit reference agency (subsection (3))`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registrar must not disclose relevant date of birth information except— (a) in accordance with subsection (2) or (3)" (an "except" once met: fork F9)
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1110F the disclosure is permitted by the registrar's general powers of disclosure`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except— ... (b) as permitted by section 1110F (general powers of disclosure by the registrar)" (an "except" once met: fork F9)
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 1110F is in another part's range (coa24)

@ref s 1087C(1) The registrar must not disclose relevant date of birth information (src:15416-15418)
`s 1087C(1) the prohibition on disclosing relevant date of birth information` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    SHANT `Action of a party` OF Registrar, Registrar, "disclose relevant date of birth information otherwise than as section 1087C(2) or (3) or section 1110F permits"
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the registrar disclosed relevant date of birth information otherwise than as permitted"

-- src:15419 | (2) The registrar may disclose relevant date of birth information if the information is made available for public inspection.
@ref s 1087C(2) The registrar may disclose information that is made available for public inspection (src:15419)
GIVEN `the relevant date of birth information is made available for public inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1087C(2) the registrar may disclose the relevant date of birth information` MEANS
    IF `the relevant date of birth information is made available for public inspection`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The registrar may disclose relevant date of birth information if the information is made available for public inspection": a grant named "may", so a failed "if" is not the text's own "may not" (fork F31)

-- src:15420 | (3) The registrar may disclose relevant date of birth information to a credit reference agency (as defined by section 243(7)).
-- src:15421 | (4) Subsections (3) to (8) of section 243 (permitted disclosure of address information by the registrar) apply for the purposes of subsection (3) as for the purposes of that section (reading references there to protected information as references to relevant date of birth information).
@ref s 1087C(3) The registrar may disclose to a credit reference agency (src:15420-15421)
GIVEN `s 243(7) the recipient is a credit reference agency` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 243(3) to (8) the conditions of those subsections, read as section 1087C(4) says, are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1087C(3) the registrar may disclose the relevant date of birth information to the recipient` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 243(7) the recipient is a credit reference agency`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `s 243(3) to (8) the conditions of those subsections, read as section 1087C(4) says, are met`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsections (3) to (8) of section 243 ... apply for the purposes of subsection (3) as for the purposes of that section"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 243 is in another part's range (coa5)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The registrar may disclose relevant date of birth information to a credit reference agency"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 243(7) is in another part's range (coa5)

-- src:15422 | (5) In this section “relevant date of birth information” has the meaning given by section 1087A(3).
@ref s 1087C(5) "relevant date of birth information" (src:15422)
GIVEN `the answer of section 1087A(3) on whether the information is relevant date of birth information` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1087C(5) the information is relevant date of birth information` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of section 1087A(3) on whether the information is relevant date of birth information`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the borrowed definition says no, supplied as an input): "“relevant date of birth information” has the meaning given by section 1087A(3)"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 1087A(3) does not decide the case

-- s 1087C(4) applies subsections (3) to (8) of section 243 for the purposes of subsection (3): the second input of s 1087C(3) above.

§§ `ss 1088 to 1092 Regulations protecting material; copies; production of records`

-- s 1088(1) to (6), (9) and (10) confer powers to make regulations, and fix their procedure: inert (reason 2).

DECLARE `s 1088(7) provision` IS ONE OF
    `s 1088(7)(a) sections 243 or 244 (or those sections as applied by section 790ZF) (residential address information)`
    `s 1088(7)(b) section 1087C(1) (disclosure of date of birth information)`
    `s 1088(7)(c) any provision of regulations under section 1046 corresponding to provision mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b)`
    `s 1088(7)(d) section 1110F (general powers of disclosure by the registrar)`
    `s 1088(7) another provision`

-- src:15442 | (7) Regulations under subsection (1)(b) or (2)(b) may not require the registrar to refrain from disclosing information under—
-- src:15443 | (a) sections 243 or 244 (or those sections as applied by section 790ZF) (residential address information);
-- src:15444 | (b) section 1087C(1) (disclosure of date of birth information);
-- src:15445 | (c) any provision of regulations under section 1046 corresponding to provision mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b);
-- src:15446 | (d) section 1110F (general powers of disclosure by the registrar).
@ref s 1088(7) Regulations may not require the registrar to refrain from disclosing under these provisions (src:15442-15446)
GIVEN p IS A `s 1088(7) provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1088(7) regulations under subsection (1)(b) or (2)(b) may require the registrar to refrain from disclosing information under the provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `s 1088(7) another provision` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar names four provisions
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Regulations under subsection (1)(b) or (2)(b) may not require the registrar to refrain from disclosing information under— (a) ... (b) ... (c) ... (d) ..."

