    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "copies are to be provided under section 1086"

-- Section 1091 skips subsection (2) in this text (the text runs (1), (3), (4), (5)); finding 14 in NOTES.md.
-- The relation of s 1091(1) is stated once, from the registrar's side (the applicant's claim to certification); the applicant's request is the input of the function and of the rule's trigger, not a second rule.
-- src:15458 | (1) A copy provided under section 1086 must be certified by the registrar as a true copy if the applicant expressly requests such certification.
@ref s 1091(1) A copy must be certified if the applicant expressly requests (src:15458)
GIVEN `the copy is provided under section 1086` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant expressly requests certification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1091(1) the registrar must certify the copy as a true copy` MEANS
    IF `the copy is provided under section 1086`
    THEN IF `the applicant expressly requests certification`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be certified by the registrar as a true copy if the applicant expressly requests such certification" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A copy provided under section 1086"

@ref s 1091(1) The registrar must certify the copy (src:15458)
`s 1091(1) the registrar's duty to certify the copy` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Registrar, Registrar, "certify the copy provided under section 1086 as a true copy"

-- src:15459 | (3) A copy provided under section 1086, certified by the registrar (whose official position it is unnecessary to prove) to be an accurate record of the contents of the original document, is in all legal proceedings admissible in evidence—
-- src:15460 | (a) as of equal validity with the original document, and
-- src:15461 | (b) as evidence (in Scotland, sufficient evidence) of any fact stated in the original document of which direct oral evidence would be admissible.
@ref s 1091(3) A certified copy is admissible in evidence (src:15459-15461)
GIVEN `the copy was provided under section 1086` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is certified by the registrar to be an accurate record of the contents of the original document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1091(3)(a) the certified copy is admissible in all legal proceedings as of equal validity with the original document` MEANS
    IF `the copy was provided under section 1086` AND `it is certified by the registrar to be an accurate record of the contents of the original document`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A copy provided under section 1086, certified by the registrar ... to be an accurate record of the contents of the original document"

DECLARE `s 1091(3)(b) weight of the evidence` IS ONE OF
    `s 1091(3)(b) evidence of the fact stated in the original document`
    `s 1091(3)(b) in Scotland, sufficient evidence of the fact stated in the original document`

@ref s 1091(3)(b) A certified copy is evidence of a fact of which direct oral evidence would be admissible (src:15459-15461)
GIVEN `the copy was provided under section 1086 and is certified by the registrar to be an accurate record of the contents of the original document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `direct oral evidence of the fact stated in the original document would be admissible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are in` IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A MAYBE (`s 1091(3)(b) weight of the evidence`)
`s 1091(3)(b) what the certified copy is as evidence of the fact` MEANS
    IF `the copy was provided under section 1086 and is certified by the registrar to be an accurate record of the contents of the original document` AND `direct oral evidence of the fact stated in the original document would be admissible`
    THEN CONSIDER `the proceedings are in`
         WHEN `Scotland` THEN JUST `s 1091(3)(b) in Scotland, sufficient evidence of the fact stated in the original document`
         OTHERWISE JUST `s 1091(3)(b) evidence of the fact stated in the original document`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "of any fact stated in the original document of which direct oral evidence would be admissible"

