-- src:15477 | (1) A person who, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply with a requirement under section 1092A commits an offence.
@ref s 1092B(1) The offence of failing to comply with a requirement under section 1092A (src:15477)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with a requirement under section 1092A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a reasonable excuse for failing to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1092B(1) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person fails to comply with a requirement under section 1092A`
    THEN IF `the person has a reasonable excuse for failing to comply`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: "without reasonable excuse"): the text does not say what follows for a person who has a reasonable excuse (fork F26)
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply with a requirement under section 1092A"

-- src:15478 | (2) Where an offence under this section is committed by a firm, an offence is also committed by every officer of the firm who is in default.
@ref s 1092B(2) An offence by a firm is also committed by every officer in default (src:15478)
GIVEN `an offence under section 1092B is committed by a firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1092B(2) an offence is also committed by the officer` MEANS
    IF `an offence under section 1092B is committed by a firm` AND `the person is an officer of the firm`
    THEN CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence is also committed by every officer of the firm who is in default"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 1121 is in another part's range (coa24)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where an offence under this section is committed by a firm"

-- The penalty of s 1092B(3), as the core's Penalty. "The general limit in a magistrates' court" is not defined in the Act: an input, in months (it is not
-- in the Act's text, and a figure from memory is not used). The fine "not exceeding the statutory maximum" is the core's fraction 1; "one-fifth of the statutory maximum" is 0.2.
-- src:15479 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:15480 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:15481 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:15482 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding the general limit in a magistrates’ court or a fine (or both);
-- src:15483 | (ii) in Scotland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both) and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-fifth of the statutory maximum;
-- src:15484 | (iii) in Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both), and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-fifth of the statutory maximum.
@ref s 1092B(3) The penalty (src:15479-15484)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of conviction`
      `the general limit in a magistrates' court, in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 1092B(3) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, JUST (Period OF 2, Years), JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, JUST (Period OF `the general limit in a magistrates' court, in months`, Months), JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, JUST (Period OF 12, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 0.2), TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 0.2), TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text gives a different penalty for each of England and Wales, Scotland and Northern Ireland, and a summary conviction in no named place is not covered
